import H0mework.Physics.FinalJoint.FixedGlobalRegularity

/-!
# Fixed P506/L0 final-common pointwise joint residual normal form

The final common action write already produces one smooth four-dimensional
configuration.  This module evaluates all nine residual channels on that
same actual at an arbitrary spacetime point.  It exposes the surviving
action terms without turning a residual coordinate, its sign, or its support
into a candidate write.

The two gravity algebraic equations vanish globally.  The Lorentz channel is
the actual torsion--coframe three-form plus matter spin.  The P286 connection
channel uses the globally constant exterior derivative generated by the
canonical affine auxiliary write.  Scalar and matter channels retain their
literal algebraic-minus-divergence action coefficients, and the coframe
channel is split into gauge plus matter minus the live constraint reaction on
the pointwise nondegenerate domain.
-/

